---
/**
 * Plain-language privacy policy TEMPLATE.
 * TODO(content): must be reviewed by the client and their lawyer before
 * launch. It describes how this site is actually built (Netlify Forms, the
 * fan list provider, Plausible, click-to-load embeds); update it if any of
 * those change.
 */
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { contact } from '@/config/site';

// TODO(content): set the date once the policy has been reviewed.
const updated = '[date of legal review]';
const provider = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_EMAIL_PROVIDER || 'netlify';
const providerName =
  provider === 'kit'
    ? 'Kit (ConvertKit)'
    : provider === 'mailchimp'
      ? 'Mailchimp'
      : 'our email provider';
const contactEmail = contact.fanEmail || contact.bookingEmail;
const sections = [
  ['who', 'Who we are'],
  ['collect', 'What we collect and why'],
  ['list', 'The fan list'],
  ['analytics', 'Analytics'],
  ['embeds', 'Music players, previews and videos'],
  ['share', 'Who we share it with'],
  ['keep', 'How long we keep it'],
  ['rights', 'Your choices and rights'],
  ['kids', 'Children'],
  ['contact', 'Contact'],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How gagemarvel.com handles your information: forms, the fan list and analytics."
>
  <header class="container-site pt-12 pb-10 lg:pt-20">
    <h1 class="page-title border-b border-charcoal-2 pb-8">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="review label mt-6">
      Draft template: to be reviewed by the client and their legal adviser before launch.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="container-site grid gap-12 pb-24 lg:grid-cols-12">
    <nav aria-label="Sections" class="lg:col-span-3">
      <ol class="toc lg:sticky lg:top-[calc(var(--header-h)+2rem)]">
        {sections.map(([id, t], i) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`#${id}`}>
              <span class="text-ivory-muted tabular-nums">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>{' '}
              {t}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <article class="prose-gm lg:col-span-8 lg:col-start-5">
      <p class="lead">
        The short version: we only collect what you choose to give us, we use it for the reason you
        gave it, we don't sell it, and we don't use advertising cookies.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ivory-muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This is the official website of Gage Marvel, an independent country music artist ("we",
        "us"). It lives at gagemarvel.com.
      </p>

      <h2 id="collect">What we collect and why</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Booking inquiries:</strong> your name, organization, email, phone, event details
          and message. Used only to respond about your event.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Fan messages:</strong> your name, email and message. Used only to read and, if we
          can, reply.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Fan list sign-ups:</strong> your email, and optionally your first name and ZIP or
          postal code. Used to send new music and show announcements, and to tell you about shows
          near you.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We don't ask for more than we need, and we never combine these with information from other
        sources.
      </p>

      <h2 id="list">The fan list</h2>
      <p>
        You join only by ticking the consent box yourself; it is never pre-ticked. We then send a
        confirmation email, and you're only added once you confirm (double opt-in). Every email has
        an unsubscribe link that works straight away. The list is managed by {providerName}.
      </p>

      <h2 id="analytics">Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use Plausible Analytics to count visits and which links get clicked (for example, which
        music service people choose). Plausible does not use cookies, does not collect personal
        information and does not track you across other websites. That's why there's no cookie
        banner.
      </p>

      <h2 id="embeds">Music players, previews and videos</h2>
      <p>
        Players from Apple Music, Spotify and YouTube don't load until you press play. Once you do,
        that service may set its own cookies under its own privacy policy. The 30 second song
        previews stream directly from Apple when you press play. Links to streaming services and
        social networks take you to those sites, which have their own policies.
      </p>

      <h2 id="share">Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We never sell your information. It's handled for us by the services that run this site:
        Netlify (hosting and forms), {providerName} (the fan list) and Plausible (analytics).
        Booking inquiries may be shared with Gage's booking and management team to arrange an event.
        We'll disclose information if the law requires it.
      </p>

      <h2 id="keep">How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Booking inquiries and messages are kept as long as needed to respond and keep a record of
        the conversation, then deleted. Fan list details are kept until you unsubscribe.
      </p>

      <h2 id="rights">Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can unsubscribe from the fan list at any time using the link in any email. You can also
        ask us to show you, correct or delete the information we hold about you. Depending on where
        you live (for example the EU, UK, Canada or California) you may have further rights under
        laws such as the GDPR, CASL or the CCPA, and you can complain to your local data protection
        authority.
      </p>

      <h2 id="kids">Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site isn't directed at children under 13 (or under 16 in the EU and UK), and we don't
        knowingly collect their information.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions or requests about your information:{' '}
        {contactEmail ? (
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>
        ) : (
          <a href="/contact#fan-message">use the fan message form</a>
        )}
        .
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-title {
    font-size: clamp(4.5rem, 18vw, 15rem);
    line-height: 0.8;
    font-weight: 900;
  }
  .review {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.7rem;
    background: var(--gold);
    color: var(--black);
  }
  .toc {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--charcoal-2);
  }
  .toc a {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--charcoal-2);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .toc a:hover {
    color: var(--gold);
  }
  .prose-gm {
    max-width: 44rem;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }
  .prose-gm .lead {
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .prose-gm h2 {
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--charcoal-2);
    font-size: 2rem;
    scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--header-h) + 1rem);
  }
  .prose-gm p,
  .prose-gm ul {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .prose-gm ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    list-style: square;
  }
  .prose-gm li::marker {
    color: var(--gold);
  }
  .prose-gm a {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .prose-gm a:hover {
    color: var(--gold);
  }
</style>
